{"artifact_id":"extract_2dfcf6b73d135f4b17a5e951","byte_end":58259,"byte_start":53951,"format_id":"reviewed-html-paragraph-v1","locator":"S3.p2.1","original_html":"<p id=\"S3.p2.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">QBH MC signal samples were generated using the <span id=\"S3.p2.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps\">QBH\u2009v3.02</span> generator <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bibx7\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">7</a>]</cite> to compute the production cross-sections and model the hard-scatter process, assuming zero angular momentum.\nEvents were then interfaced to <span id=\"S3.p2.1.2\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps\">Pythia</span>\u20098 <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bibx35\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">35</a>]</cite> to model parton showering and hadronisation.\nAs in previous iterations of searches for QBHs, the CTEQ6L1 <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bibx36\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">36</a>]</cite> PDF set was used and the QCD factorisation scale set to the inverse gravitational radius <cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bibx7\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">7</a>]</cite>.\nRequiring the QBH mass to be in the range <math id=\"S3.p2.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"(1{-}3)M_{\\textrm{th}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>\u2212</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">\u200b</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(1{-}3)M_{\\textrm{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> (with <math id=\"S3.p2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"M_{\\textrm{th}}=M_{\\textrm{D}}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>D</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M_{\\textrm{th}}=M_{\\textrm{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>) ensures that QBHs are produced in a region where quantum effects are significant, excluding thermal decays.\nIn the ADD model, <math id=\"S3.p2.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"n=2,4,\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=2,4,</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id=\"S3.p2.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"6\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">6</annotation></semantics></math> EDs are assumed, whereas <math id=\"S3.p2.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"n=1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n=1</annotation></semantics></math> is used in the RS model.\nThe kinematic distributions of the decay products are governed by the QBH mass; consequently, the signal acceptance and reconstruction efficiency are found to be independent of the specific model type or the number of extra dimensions.\nThe production cross-section is significantly lower for the RS model than for the ADD model. Samples were produced in <math id=\"S3.p2.m6\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"0.5\\penalty\\ \\textrm{TeV}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace=\"0.500em\" rspace=\"0em\">\u200b</mo><mtext>TeV</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0.5\\penalty\\ \\textrm{TeV}</annotation></semantics></math> steps through threshold mass ranges of <math id=\"S3.p2.m7\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"M_{\\textrm{th}}\\in[6,8.5]\\penalty\\ \\textrm{TeV}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msub><mo>\u2208</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.500em\" rspace=\"0em\">\u200b</mo><mtext>TeV</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">M_{\\textrm{th}}\\in[6,8.5]\\penalty\\ \\textrm{TeV}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id=\"S3.p2.m8\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"[8,10.5]\\penalty\\ \\textrm{TeV}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.500em\" rspace=\"0em\">\u200b</mo><mtext>TeV</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[8,10.5]\\penalty\\ \\textrm{TeV}</annotation></semantics></math> for the RS and ADD models, respectively.</p>","parser_version":"1.0.0","purpose":"RESEARCH","review_status":"PROPOSED","schema_version":"1.0.0","source_hash":"6871595fe1a737fb5cdcc57f322626d870b24a7afc3060feb3ec4a9186c10444","source_id":"atlas_paper_v2","source_version":"2604.19495v2"}